# "Mit Zäsur würde <ref target="#example7">das</ref> gehen" pointed at
# <notatedMusic xml:id="example7"> (the student's example7.xml), which was lost
# when notatedMusic became kinesic/desc/ptr[@type="transcription"] (30106ef).
# No element carries that ID any more; example7.xml has no xml:ids.
encodings/4/hill/comments_de.xml: #example7

# --- No. 5, 1731: fourth Presto not encoded -----------------------------------
# "Wo das Presto befindlich" points to all Presto marks. The print has four
# (bars 1, 10, 20 and one after the adagio on p. 327); score.xml encodes only
# presto-000..presto-002. Needs a <tempo xml:id="presto-003"> in the MEI.
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_de.xml: #presto-003

# --- No. 11: the staves of bars 23 and 24 have no IDs --------------------------
# The 1719 text refers to the bass staff of bars 23 and 24 (3rd and 4th bar of
# the second part), but in score.xml their <staff> elements (and everything
# inside them) carry no xml:id, and never did in this repository. The measures
# got their IDs back from the music examples, which point to them. Fix in the
# MEI: in bar 23, staff n="2" xml:id="staff-0000000633397600"; in bar 24,
# staff n="2" xml:id="staff-0000001023194498" (their zones exist already).
encodings/11/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: #staff-0000000633397600
encodings/11/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: #staff-0000001023194498
